Spec: Cross-platform conformance vectors

Purpose:
  Preserve exact public-contract input bytes and expected outcomes for independent parsers.

Owns:
  ./cases.json
  ./generate.py

References:
  /docs/adr/0001-public-contract-normalization.md

Must:
  Include independently specified status and operation cases covering lifecycle, uint64, timestamp and fixed-error boundaries.
  Encode input bytes as `inputUtf8Base64` so malformed encoding and duplicate keys remain representable.
  Specify `kind`, `id`, `accepted` and either `normalized` or `errorCode` per case.
  Include explicit cases for budgets, lexical integers, duplicate keys, malformed Unicode and authority boundaries.
  Connection request cases may carry a separate `approvedPolicyUtf8Base64`; expected normalized output includes the request and `withinApproved` without treating comparison as actual authorization.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Publish reviewed valid and invalid manifest and standalone-policy cases.

Done when:
  Both language runners consume this same corpus and agree with its expected outcomes.
